{
  "title": "This Telugu director opines that commercial films are not made for intellectuals",
  "publication_date": "2025-04-18T04:45:47+00:00",
  "summary": "Director Pradeep Chilukuri, whose film Arjun S/o Vyjayanthi starring Nandamuri Kalyan Ram, Vijayashanthi and Saiee Manjrekar is now in theatres, says commercial films are made for a different audience and \"are not made for intellectuals.\" He expects viewers to connect with the film's mother-son sentiment.",
  "content": "Nandamuri Kalyan Ram\u2019s Arjun S/o Vyjayanthi is now out in theatres. The emotional action drama rides heavily on mother-son sentiment. Lady Superstar Vijayashanthi played Kalyan Ram\u2019s mother. Saiee Manjrekar is the female lead. Pradeep Chilukuri, who earlier made Raja Cheyyi Vesthe, is the director.\n\nDuring an interview, a journalist told Pradeep that the commercial cinema trope where the hero first acts as a criminal and later turns a cop has been overused. The director replied, \"I am not at all worried about this aspect. Intellectual people criticize filmmakers who make commercial movies and often label them as run-of-the-mill directors.\"\n\nPradeep Chilukuri added, \"Commercial films have a different set of audience. They are not made for intellectuals. Our Arjun S/o Vyjayanthi\u2019s target audience is different. I am sure they will surely connect to mother and son\u2019s emotion.\" This is an interesting statement from the young director and let\u2019s see how the film fares at the box office.",
